      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="-548596004">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Header</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">HINT</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195997">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip1</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US">Using the March action is generally the only way to get your figures to Yggdrasil, since you can't normally invade Yggdrasil.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="-755748851">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip10</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">Remember that for each fight you win, you need to discard a card (if you still have any). So make sure you can afford to lose the cards you have.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195996">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip2</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">There are no villages in Yggdrasil, so there is no limit to the number of figures you can have there.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195995">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip3</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">Be aware of the danger of your opponent playing Loki's Trickery and only have 1 Rage left, thus ending your turn.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195994">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip4</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">When you have 0 remaining Rage, you can use Loki's Trickery to gain 1 Rage, and be back in the game.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195993">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip5</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">Frigga's Protection can be a powerful insurance against Odin's Tide!</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195992">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip6</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">By starting a fight, you can move your figures via 'Call to Battle' for free.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195991">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip7</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US">In bigger games, be aware that your opponent's might play multiple copies of Loki cards, resulting in huge losses of Rage or Glory.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195990">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip8</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">Keep in mind that many of the Warrior upgrades also increase the cost of your Warriors.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2" id="281195989">
        <source>LoadingScreen.Hint.Tip9</source>
        <target xml:lang="en-US" xmlns="urn:oasis:names:tc:xliff:document:1.2">When keeping powerful figures like the Troll or Soldier of Hel in reserve, beware of your figure limit and be sure that you can still place figures.</target>
      </trans-unit>
